  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="e36b-f568-1839-65d7" name="Byzantine (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>BYZANTINE ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.28-29), 7th-11th centuries AD.
Characters: the army may have a General and an Army Standard Bearer. Cavalry at least a quarter of the points; Infantry up to three quarters; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to a quarter, with one artillery piece per 500 points.
Combined Formations: skutatoi may be combined with archers into one regiment (archers in the rear ranks, losing light infantry status), and cataphracts may include bow-armed models in the same unit (the Cataphract Archers entry; they must be combined with Cataphracts). Casualties are taken from the front rank first. Not enforced; field the pieces as separate units and combine them on the table.
Strategicon (choose one at the start of battle if the army has a General): Flank March (play the Flank Attack scenario as the flankers), Hidden Ambush Force (one unit set up in hiding, out of sight of the opponent's deployment zone, deployed at the start of your first turn) or Scouts (your opponent sets up first).
Allies (not built here: make a separate small roster): troops from the Cataphract and/or Nomadic Hordes lists.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Infantry: up to 75%
  Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
